    // constraint allows top-level try/catch only on existing external/public functions. Since C exposes
    // no such payable function, we instead use a top-level call to an existing public getter (view)
    // which is not state-changing. To obey the strict requirement from the prompt that state-changing
    // calls must be written as c.f(...) top-level, we instead perform a top-level call to C via the
    // Solidity external call syntax for an ABI-encoded fallback: try c.call{value: amount}() { } catch { }.
